      ],
      "bounds": "Two concurrent waiters, one shared or two separate producers, one replacement; transport and immutable domains; five contexts; immutable registry limit 1 or 2 with unit-weight producers. This bounds admitted unfinished shared producers, including slow finalizers, not all independent fallback requests. Equality abstracts the complete credential/origin/version/physical Store/fixed owner+snapshot+content/read-only/policy/timeout/scheduler identity.",
      "scope": "Transport coalescers remain service local. Only exact immutable network bytes in one Node process may cross standard SDK runtime boundaries. Each caller independently qualifies its original pin/current owner and persists to its own Store; the producer owns its own read-only transport Scope and no Store. Custom transports and opt-in RequestBudget bypass cross-runtime sharing. No cross-process content sharing. Effect dependency scope is reference counting and entry-identity removal only."
    },
    "RequestAdmission": {
      "kind": "bounded_admission_and_retry",
      "symbols": [
        "makeRequestScheduler.schedule",
        "NotionTransport.request once/execute",
        "makeRequestBudget",
        "withinRequestBudget",
        "isRetryableNotionWriteRejection"
      ],
      "bounds": "One invocation with opt-in budget, two admitted attempts, four clock ticks, short/long queue window, one-tick attempt timer; read and mutating request variants.",
      "scope": "Shared SQL claims are abstract atomic decisions. No proof of SQLite driver/crash, arbitrary clocks, all rate-limit scopes, byte serialization, or cross-machine coordination."
    }
